WEBVTT

00:00:08.061 --> 00:00:10.281
[crowd cheering]

00:00:11.674 --> 00:00:13.501
TROLL: All right,
where do we put these things?

00:00:13.545 --> 00:00:15.068
TROLL 2:
I need a circuit hookup.

00:00:15.112 --> 00:00:17.462
[quietly]: Okay, come on.
Let's go, let's go, let's go.

00:00:17.505 --> 00:00:20.857
[bells jingling quietly]

00:00:22.162 --> 00:00:24.643
Hey. Stop right there.

00:00:24.687 --> 00:00:26.036
[jingling stops]

00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:27.864
BIGGIE: Legsly, I told you
not to wear your anklet.

00:00:27.907 --> 00:00:30.823
Only Rock Trolls
are allowed back here.

00:00:30.867 --> 00:00:34.566
Well, it's funny
you should mention that,

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.440
because we are genuine
Hard Rockers.

00:00:39.484 --> 00:00:41.747
[electric guitar strums weakly]

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:44.228
[deep voice]:
One, two, three, four!

00:00:44.271 --> 00:00:45.664
-♪ Rainbows, unicorns
-[heavy metal music playing]

00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:47.361
♪ Everything nice, yeah

00:00:47.405 --> 00:00:49.015
♪ Sugarplums, fairy dust

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:51.714
♪ Everything nice, yeah

00:00:51.757 --> 00:00:54.238
-♪ Brush your teeth.
-[hat squeaks]

00:00:55.631 --> 00:00:56.762
Cool.

00:00:56.806 --> 00:00:59.156
Hurry up.
The show's about to start, man.

00:00:59.199 --> 00:01:00.897
Queen Barb's
about to go onstage.

00:01:03.073 --> 00:01:04.335
We're screwed.

00:01:04.378 --> 00:01:06.598
-[rock music playing]
-[crowd cheering]

00:01:08.861 --> 00:01:10.341
BARB:
So, Popcorn,

00:01:10.384 --> 00:01:11.908
is being my best friend

00:01:11.951 --> 00:01:13.823
everything you could have
ever dreamed of?

00:01:13.866 --> 00:01:16.042
-[grunts]
-[Barb and Trolls laugh]

00:01:16.086 --> 00:01:17.653
I am not your best friend.

00:01:17.696 --> 00:01:20.438
You don't have to be
embarrassed. I get it.

00:01:20.481 --> 00:01:22.875
Being queen
can be kind of lonely.

00:01:22.919 --> 00:01:25.399
CROWD [chanting]:
Barb! Barb! Barb! Barb! Barb!

00:01:25.443 --> 00:01:27.793
[chanting fades]

00:01:27.837 --> 00:01:30.970
There's all this pressure
to be a great queen.

00:01:32.972 --> 00:01:35.453
And instead of real friends,
you're just surrounded by

00:01:35.496 --> 00:01:38.848
people who just tell you
what you want to hear.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.547
You know, other than
your terrible taste in music

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:45.245
and clothing
and general lifestyle,

00:01:45.289 --> 00:01:47.639
you and me are the same,
Popsqueak.

00:01:47.683 --> 00:01:49.032
Uh... [scoffs]
No, we're not.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.599
We're both queens who just
want to unite the world.

00:01:51.643 --> 00:01:53.253
You don't want
to unite the world.

00:01:53.297 --> 00:01:54.777
You want to destroy it!

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.256
Nuh-uh. No way.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.476
No. I don't know
who told you that.

00:01:58.519 --> 00:02:01.609
Music has done nothing
but divide us.

00:02:01.653 --> 00:02:03.742
Now that I have
the final string,

00:02:03.786 --> 00:02:07.964
I can make us all one nation
of Trolls, under rock.

00:02:08.007 --> 00:02:09.617
[guitar roars]

00:02:09.661 --> 00:02:11.794
[magic jingling, whooshing]

00:02:14.274 --> 00:02:15.885
[pop riff plays]

00:02:22.979 --> 00:02:25.111
[rock riff echoes]

00:02:25.155 --> 00:02:26.286
[laughs]

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.723
What are you gonna do?

00:02:27.766 --> 00:02:30.334
Play the ultimate power chord,
and then...

00:02:30.377 --> 00:02:31.509
[chuckles]

00:02:31.552 --> 00:02:33.337
You'll see!

00:02:37.558 --> 00:02:39.560
-["Barracuda" playing]
-[crowd cheering]

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.699
[crowd grunting in unison
to rhythm]

00:02:47.743 --> 00:02:50.789
-♪ Queen Barb!
-[crowd cheering]

00:02:50.833 --> 00:02:52.791
♪ So this ain't the end

00:02:52.835 --> 00:02:57.230
♪ I saw you again today

00:02:57.274 --> 00:03:00.407
♪ I had to turn my heart away

00:03:00.451 --> 00:03:02.366
[crowd grunting in unison
to rhythm]

00:03:02.409 --> 00:03:04.368
♪ Smile like the sun

00:03:04.411 --> 00:03:08.676
♪ Kisses for everyone

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:11.505
♪ And tales, it never fails

00:03:11.549 --> 00:03:13.159
[crowd grunting in unison
to rhythm]

00:03:13.203 --> 00:03:16.815
♪ You're lying so low
in the weeds ♪

00:03:16.859 --> 00:03:19.818
-♪ I bet you gonna ambush me
-Rock on!

00:03:19.862 --> 00:03:20.993
Rock on!

00:03:21.037 --> 00:03:23.648
♪ You'd have me
down, down, down, down ♪

00:03:23.691 --> 00:03:25.563
♪ Down on my knees

00:03:25.606 --> 00:03:28.044
♪ Now, won't ya?

00:03:28.087 --> 00:03:29.959
[music and cheering stop]

00:03:31.699 --> 00:03:34.833
♪ Barracuda!

00:03:34.877 --> 00:03:36.835
-[music resumes]
-[crowd cheering]

00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:38.750
[laughs] Bam!

00:03:40.578 --> 00:03:42.841
-[playing note rhythmically]
-Hey! Look, Daddy!

00:03:42.885 --> 00:03:44.800
I'm a rock star!

00:03:44.843 --> 00:03:48.281
Uh, this is a little hot.

00:03:48.325 --> 00:03:50.370
[chuckles]

00:03:50.414 --> 00:03:51.371
[crowd cheering]

00:03:51.415 --> 00:03:54.592
[electricity booming]

00:03:57.769 --> 00:03:59.249
[crowd cheering, whooping]

00:03:59.292 --> 00:04:01.381
Give it up
for your former leaders.

00:04:01.425 --> 00:04:05.516
Funk, Country,
Techno, Classical...

00:04:05.559 --> 00:04:07.213
[crowd booing]

00:04:07.257 --> 00:04:09.737
...and worst of all, Pop.

00:04:09.781 --> 00:04:11.087
[booing continues]

00:04:15.004 --> 00:04:16.744
[electrical crackling,
whooshing]

00:04:16.788 --> 00:04:20.661
Who wants to see what the
ultimate power chord can do?

00:04:20.705 --> 00:04:22.620
[crowd cheering, whooping]

00:04:25.057 --> 00:04:26.232
No. No!

00:04:26.276 --> 00:04:27.625
[playing rock riff]

00:04:27.668 --> 00:04:29.845
[chuckles, grunts]

00:04:31.107 --> 00:04:32.630
[grunts]

00:04:35.938 --> 00:04:37.591
[Sheila B whoops]

00:04:37.635 --> 00:04:40.594
Ha! I guess a giant
comprehensive manual

00:04:40.638 --> 00:04:42.335
does come in handy.

00:04:42.379 --> 00:04:44.381
Bla-dow! Just in time!

00:04:44.424 --> 00:04:45.382
Branch!

00:04:45.425 --> 00:04:46.862
Well, isn't that puke.

00:04:46.905 --> 00:04:49.995
Poppy's little boyfriend
came to crash the concert.

00:04:50.039 --> 00:04:51.779
Too late, Branch.

00:04:51.823 --> 00:04:53.042
Wait!

00:05:00.136 --> 00:05:01.137
Branch!

00:05:05.837 --> 00:05:07.360
[crowd murmuring quietly]

00:05:07.404 --> 00:05:08.796
No.

00:05:14.237 --> 00:05:16.239
[crackling]

00:05:19.503 --> 00:05:20.983
Branch.

00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:25.248
Rock on!

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:27.076
[crowd cheering]

00:05:27.119 --> 00:05:29.556
Oh, sick! Totally works.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.558
Who's ready to get
rippin' tattoos

00:05:31.602 --> 00:05:34.953
everywhere but our faces in
case we still need office jobs?

00:05:34.997 --> 00:05:36.172
Rah!

00:05:36.215 --> 00:05:38.696
You're turning everyone
into rock zombies?

00:05:38.739 --> 00:05:41.829
Yep. I can't wait
to party with you, Poppy.

00:05:41.873 --> 00:05:45.094
[rock music playing]

